  "bug_report_content": "Title: MathUtils.gcd(Integer.MIN_VALUE, 0) should throw an Exception instead of returning Integer.MIN_VALUE\nType: Bug | Priority: Minor | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nThe gcd method should throw an Exception for gcd(Integer.MIN_VALUE, 0), like for gcd(Integer.MIN_VALUE, Integer.MIN_VALUE). The method should only return nonnegative results.\n\nComments:\n\n[Christian Semrau]: Attached is a patch for gcd, and also for lcm, which failed for some special cases: lcm failed for (0,0) and for (Integer.MIN_VALUE, power of 2).\n\nI also added Javadoc for special cases.\n\n[Luc Maisonobe]: Fixed in trunk as of r746511.\nThanks for the patch",
